    {
      "id": "step-1.1",
      "claim": "Direct algebra gives $|h(x)-h(y)|\\le2|x-y|$, so $h$ is uniformly continuous; its displayed inverse and the usual open-interval formulas make it a homeomorphism. [L1, L2]",
      "step": "1.1",
      "inputs": [
        "L1",
        "L2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "step-1.2",
      "claim": "Put $a_n=n/(n+1)$ and $b_n=(n+1)/(n+2)$. Then $|a_n-b_n|\\to0$, while $|h^{-1}(a_n)-h^{-1}(b_n)|=1$. [L2, L3]",
      "step": "1.2",
      "inputs": [
        "L2",
        "L3"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "step-2.1",
      "claim": "Thus $h^{-1}$ is not uniformly continuous, so this homeomorphism is not a uniform isomorphism ([[def-uniform-embedding-and-uniform-isomorphism]], [[def-homeomorphism-and-open-maps]]). [step 1.1, step 1.2] ∎",
      "step": "2.1",
      "inputs": [
