      "id": "step-2.3",
      "claim": "Start instead with a uniform-cover structure. The $E_{\\mathcal V}$-ball at $x$ is $$ E_{\\mathcal V}[x]=\\operatorname{St}(x,\\mathcal V), $$ the union of the members of $\\mathcal V$ containing $x$. Thus $\\mathcal V$ refines $\\mathcal C_{E_{\\mathcal V}}$, so the latter is uniform by coarsening. Conversely, if $\\mathcal W$ star-refines $\\mathcal V$, then for any $x$ and any $W_0\\in\\mathcal W$ containing $x$, $\\operatorname{St}(x,\\mathcal W)\\subseteq\\operatorname{St}(W_0,\\mathcal W)$, which lies in some member of $\\mathcal V$. Therefore $\\mathcal C_{E_{\\mathcal W}}$ refines $\\mathcal V$. The recovered cover structure is exactly the original one. [L2, step 1.2]",
