      "inputs": [
        "L2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "step-1.2",
      "claim": "Conversely, if $x\\in U$ is original-open, apply [L1] to the closed set $X\\setminus U$ to obtain $f$ with $f(x)=1$ and $f[X\\setminus U]=\\{0\\}$; then the $p_f$-ball of radius $1/2$ about $x$ lies in $U$. [L1, L3, choose]",
      "step": "1.2",
