items/lem-metric-uniformity-dictionary.md:44:1.1 The diagonal lies in every $E_\varepsilon$, inverses agree with $E_\varepsilon$ by symmetry, intersections contain $E_{\min(\varepsilon,\delta)}$, and $E_{\varepsilon/2}\circ E_{\varepsilon/2}\subseteq E_\varepsilon$ by the triangle inequality. [L1]
