 ## Statement
 
-The topology of a completely regular space is induced by the gauge of pseudometrics $p_f(x,y)=|f(x)-f(y)|$, where $f:X\to[0,1]$ ranges over continuous maps.
+The topology of a nonempty completely regular space is induced by the gauge of pseudometrics $p_f(x,y)=|f(x)-f(y)|$, where $f:X\to[0,1]$ ranges over continuous maps.
 
 ## Facts & Assumptions
 
-**Given:** A completely regular space $X$.
+**Given:** A nonempty completely regular space $X$.
 
