 ## Definition
 
-A **gauge of pseudometrics** on $X$ is a family $\mathcal P$ of pseudometrics ([[def-metric-space]]). For finite $F\subseteq\mathcal P$ and $\varepsilon>0$, put $E(F,\varepsilon)=\{(x,y):p(x,y)<\varepsilon\text{ for every }p\in F\}$. The nonempty such sets form a filter base and generate a uniformity ([[def-filter-base]], [[lem-filter-base-generates]]), called the uniformity **generated by $\mathcal P$**.
+A **gauge of pseudometrics** on $X$ is a family $\mathcal P$ of pseudometrics ([[def-metric-space]]). For finite $F\subseteq\mathcal P$ and $\varepsilon>0$, put $E(F,\varepsilon)=\{(x,y):p(x,y)<\varepsilon\text{ for every }p\in F\}$. If $X\ne\varnothing$, these sets form a filter base and generate a uniformity ([[def-filter-base]], [[lem-filter-base-generates]]), called the uniformity **generated by $\mathcal P$**.
 
