items/def-separated-uniform-space.md:28:A uniformity $\mathcal U$ on $X$ is **separated** when $\bigcap_{E\in\mathcal U}E=\Delta_X$ ([[def-the-diagonal-of-a-space]]). Equivalently, whenever $x\ne y$, some entourage $E$ satisfies $(x,y)\notin E$. Separation is a property of the uniformity, not an additional convention in the meaning of uniform space.
